# Tables intentionally excluded from scripts/check_rls_coverage.py.
#
# One table name per line, `#` for comments. Every entry here needs a comment
# explaining *why* it's safe for a school_id-bearing table to have RLS off,
# or to have policies that don't reference auth_school_id()/auth_is_super_admin()
# -- same convention as .anon_execute_definer_allowlist.
#
# Empty on purpose as of the 2026-09-14 production-readiness audit: the sample
# of tables checked by hand during that audit (students, invoices, payments,
# marks, student_attendance, school_users, supplier_invoices) all reference
# auth_school_id()/auth_is_super_admin() directly, so the first real run of
# this check is expected to either come back clean or surface something that
# genuinely needs a look -- not something to pre-allowlist speculatively.
# Reviewed 2026-11-05 against production's actual policy and function definitions.
#
# These ten tables have RLS on and a SELECT policy that does not name auth_school_id() directly.
# Each policy calls a SECURITY DEFINER helper (fixed search_path, STABLE) whose body begins with
# `p_school = auth_school_id()`, so tenant scoping is enforced one call away. The checker only
# greps the policy text, so it cannot see through the helper. Recheck a helper here if its
# definition ever changes.
#
# canteen_staff_can_read(school) = school = auth_school_id() AND flag feature.canteen.stores
#                                  AND auth_has_permission('canteen.read')
# canteen_can_see_student(school, student) = school = auth_school_id() AND flag feature.canteen.stores
#                                  AND (canteen.read OR guardian of student OR the student themself)
canteen_items
canteen_stock_movements
canteen_sales
canteen_wallets
canteen_wallet_entries
# Child of canteen_sales: the policy is EXISTS (select 1 from canteen_sales ...), and the parent's
# own RLS applies inside that subquery, so a row is visible only if its parent sale is.
canteen_sale_lines
#
# learning_can_see_stream(school, stream) = school = auth_school_id() AND flag feature.learning.portal
#                                  AND (academics.read OR guardian of a student in the stream
#                                       OR a student in the stream)
learning_quizzes
learning_resources
tutor_drafts
